sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant In as Input splits
    participant M as Mappers
    participant Sh as Shuffle
    participant R as Reducers
    participant Out as Output
    In->>M: one split per mapper, near the data
    Note over In,M: move compute to the data — the shuffle is the expensive part, not the read
    M->>M: combine locally before emitting
    Note over M: a combiner cuts shuffle volume, which is usually the whole bottleneck
    M->>Sh: partitioned, sorted output
    Sh->>R: fetch each partition
    alt one key dominates
        R-->>Sh: that reducer runs long after the others finish
        Note over Sh,R: skew — salt the key or partition it further
    end
    R->>Out: write
